  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThis relates to the change made in the HTML standard stemming from https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7473 where the intent appears to have been to special case skip navigation in the location hash setter if it did not change.\n\nUnfortunately, I don't believe the spec prose fully matches the intent of that change in the case of `location.hash = \"\"`. This is as the current URL may have a fragment of \"null\" while copyURL will end up having the fragment of the empty string after the parse.\n\nThis results in a mismatch between the WPT test https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/hash-empty-string.html and the specification.\n\nI would have just submitted a PR to the HTML spec fixing this to match all browsers behavior regarding that test, but this section of the spec relates to another WPT test that matches current spec prose (https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location_hash_set_empty_string.html) which browsers disagree on.\n\nSo raising this issue to try and figure out whether specification and the WPT test location_hash_set_empty_string.html should change, or just the specification.\n",
